{"causes": ["The emergence of humanism in Classical Greece emphasized the importance of individual achievement and physical beauty.", "The establishment of the Olympic Games around 776 BCE created a cultural context that celebrated athletic prowess and competition.", "Lysippos' innovative techniques in sculpture marked a departure from earlier rigid styles, paving the way for more dynamic representations of the human form."], "effects": ["The Apoxyomenos influenced subsequent generations of sculptors, particularly during the Renaissance, by serving as a model for naturalistic representation of the human body.", "Its discovery contributed to the understanding of Hellenistic art and the cultural values associated with athleticism in ancient Greece.", "The statue has become a symbol of the enduring legacy of Greek art and its impact on Western culture, particularly in the realms of sport and aesthetics."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "lysippos", "sourceName": "Lysippos", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "apoxyomenos", "targetName": "Apoxyomenos", "context": "Lysippos sculpted the Apoxyomenos around 330 BCE, showcasing his revolutionary approach to art."}, {"sourceSlug": "ancient-greece", "sourceName": "Ancient Greece", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "apoxyomenos", "targetName": "Apoxyomenos", "context": "Ancient Greek ideals of beauty and athleticism heavily influenced the design and significance of the Apoxyomenos."}, {"sourceSlug": "olympic-games", "sourceName": "Olympic Games", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "apoxyomenos", "targetName": "Apoxyomenos", "context": "The Apoxyomenos reflects the cultural values celebrated during the Olympic Games of ancient Greece."}, {"sourceSlug": "roman-copies", "sourceName": "Roman Copies", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "apoxyomenos", "targetName": "Apoxyomenos", "context": "Roman copies of the Apoxyomenos helped transmit Greek artistic ideals to later cultures."}, {"sourceSlug": "classical-art", "sourceName": "Classical Art", "verb": "DEFINES", "targetSlug": "apoxyomenos", "targetName": "Apoxyomenos", "context": "The Apoxyomenos is a defining example of Classical art, representing the transition to a more naturalistic style."}], "places": [{"name": "Lošinj, Croatia", "role": "Discovery site"}, {"name": "Athens, Greece", "role": "Cultural center"}, {"name": "Olympia, Greece", "role": "Site of the Olympic Games"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Apoxyomenos", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "apoxyomenos"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q431029", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apoxyomenos"], "tags": ["sculpture", "Sculpture & Monuments", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Apoxyomenos contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Influenced artistic traditions and cultural expression. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The Apoxyomenos significantly influenced the development of Western art by embodying the Classical ideals of beauty and athleticism, impacting both ancient and modern representations of the human form.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-30T21:14:37Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28475993084", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Sculpture by lysippos Created by Lysippos. Dating to c. 330 BCE.", "newValue": "The Apoxyomenos, a remarkable bronze statue created by the renowned sculptor Lysippos around 330 BCE, epitomizes the artistic and cultural advancements of the Classical era in ancient Greece. This masterpiece represents an athlete scraping sweat and dirt from his body after competition, a testament to the significance of athleticism and physical beauty in Greek society. Originating from the Hellenistic period, the sculpture reflects the shift towards more naturalistic forms and dynamic poses in Greek art, influenced by the ideals of humanism and the celebration of the body.

Lysippos, a pivotal figure in the artistic landscape of his time, was known for his innovative approach to proportion and movement, which was a departure from the rigid styles of his predecessors. The Apoxyomenos was part of a broader trend in the 4th century BCE where sculptors began to emphasize individuality and emotion in their works. The statue's discovery in the 19th century, particularly the finding of a Roman copy in 1896 on the Croatian island of Lošinj, ignited scholarly interest and provided insights into ancient Greek artistic practices and the cultural values surrounding athletic competition.

The legacy of the Apoxyomenos extends beyond its aesthetic beauty; it has influenced generations of artists and sculptors who have drawn inspiration from its form and subject matter. The statue is emblematic of the ideals of the Olympic Games and the broader Greek cultural emphasis on physical excellence, which persisted through the ages, impacting the Renaissance and continuing into modern representations of athleticism. Moreover, it serves as a cultural artifact that connects contemporary audiences to the values and practices of ancient Greece, affirming the significance of sports and competition in human history."}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-30T21:14:37Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28475993084", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Artistic and cultural expression in sculptural tradition"], "newValue": ["The emergence of humanism in Classical Greece emphasized the importance of individual achievement and physical beauty.", "The establishment of the Olympic Games around 776 BCE created a cultural context that celebrated athletic prowess and competition.", "Lysippos' innovative techniques in sculpture marked a departure from earlier rigid styles, paving the way for more dynamic representations of the human form."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-30T21:14:37Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28475993084", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Influenced artistic traditions and cultural expression"], "newValue": ["The Apoxyomenos influenced subsequent generations of sculptors, particularly during the Renaissance, by serving as a model for naturalistic representation of the human body.", "Its discovery contributed to the understanding of Hellenistic art and the cultural values associated with athleticism in ancient Greece.", "The statue has become a symbol of the enduring legacy of Greek art and its impact on Western culture, particularly in the realms of sport and aesthetics."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-30T21:14:37Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH